==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno}}, from {{etyl|fro}} ''tenement'', from {{ML.}} ''[[tenementum]]'', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[tenere]]''.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
'''tenement'''

# a [[building]] that is [[rented]] to [[multiple]] [[tenant]]s, especially a low-rent, run-down one
# {{legal}}  Property, such as land, rents, or franchises, held by one person leasing it from another.
[Middle English, house, from Old French, from Medieval Latin tenēmentum, from Latin tenēre, to hold.]


